# 6. Privacy-Focused Browsers

Privacy-focused browsers are browsers designed to reduce tracking, fingerprinting, unwanted advertisements, or unnecessary data collection.

### Privacy Mechanism

Depending on the browser, privacy features may include:

* Tracker blocking
* Cookie controls
* Fingerprinting protections
* HTTPS enforcement
* Private browsing features
* Reduced third-party tracking

### Advantages

* Reduces web tracking.
* Can block many third-party trackers.
* Provides users with greater control over browser privacy.
* Easy to use compared with some network-level privacy tools.

### Limitations

* Cannot provide complete anonymity.
* Websites may still identify users through accounts or other information.
* Some privacy features can cause website compatibility problems.
* Browser privacy does not protect all other applications on the device.

### Appropriate Use Cases

* Everyday private browsing
* Reducing advertising tracking
* Limiting third-party trackers
* Improving browser privacy

